    11→    \centering
    12→    \includegraphics[width=1\linewidth]{images/overall_methodology.png}
    13→    \caption{The model consists of dual-path CNN backbones with modality-specific attention (CBAM for Sentinel-1 SAR, ECA for Sentinel-2 optical) that extract multi-scale   features through four stages (64, 128, 256, 512 channels). Shallow Feature Fusion (SFF) modules merge  cross-modal information at each scale, with skip connections (orange dashed arrows) propagating  multi-resolution features to the decoder. Three novel contributions are highlighted: (1) Multi-Resolution  Processing enables training on coarse 60m labels while processing fine 10-20m inputs through learned  adaptive aggregation and guided disaggregation, (2) the Fusion Vision Transformer (FVit) employs learnable  adaptive fusion weights ($\lambda_{sa}$, $\lambda_{ca}$) in its Ada-MBA stage to dynamically balance  self-attention and cross-attention based on data quality, and (3) Quality-Aware Training incorporates cloud   masks and quality flags through confidence-weighted loss with curriculum learning. The decoder produces  dual outputs: fractional snow cover prediction $\hat{y}$ and uncertainty estimate $\sigma^2$.}
